-- `unknown_markup_lowering` (boundary.md §9.2): a platform's `"markup"`
-- `"lowering"` names a lowering compiled into this beni, and this one names
-- `nope`, which no beni has. It is refused when the platform is loaded,
-- against the manifest that names it at 1:1 with no excerpt, whether or not
-- the program writes markup.
import Prog exposing (Program)


main : Program
main =
    Prog.say "hello"
